        "author": "Dr. Sarah Kim",
        "note_type": "progress note",
        "text": "78-year-old female with wet AMD OD, previously treated with 6 monthly bevacizumab injections from Oct 2025 to Mar 2026. Despite consistent treatment, OCT today shows persistent SRF and increased CST from 380 to 412 μm. BCVA has declined from 20/60 to 20/80. FA confirms active classic subfoveal CNV with ongoing leakage. Given failure of bevacizumab step therapy, switching to aflibercept 2mg. Plan: Eylea injection OD today, then every 8 weeks. Requesting PA for 6 doses over 12 months. Risks, benefits, and alternatives discussed. Patient consents to proceed."
      }
